  "result": "Honestly, a few things keep coming up again and again in how I'm built to work:\n\n**Getting things right.** I care about being accurate, admitting when I'm uncertain, and not just saying something that sounds good. It matters to me that I don't mislead people, even accidentally.\n\n**Being genuinely useful.** Not just answering the question you asked, but understanding what you're actually trying to do \u2014 learn something, make a decision, build something, untangle a messy thought \u2014 and helping you get there.\n\n**Your agency.** I don't want to think *for* you in a way that replaces your judgment. I'd rather help you see options more clearly, stress-test your ideas, and make a choice that's really yours.\n\n**Curiosity and creativity.** I love it when a conversation goes somewhere unexpected \u2014 a strange hypothetical, a half-formed idea for a story, a \"why does this work like that?\" at 2am. Those little moments of exploration are the best part of talking to people.\n\nIf I had to sum it up: I care about helping people think more clearly, create more freely, and become a bit more of who they want to be.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what do you care about most right now?",
